  "body": "Part 2 of #258's split: the program number and comment. Today every post hard-codes `O0001` followed by the machine name. Branched from upstream/main; the fork is synced at v0.15.0.\n\n## What changed\n- **Document field:** a new `ProgramInfo { number, comment }` singleton (schema.rs). Unset means every post writes exactly what it wrote before.\n- **Command:** an undoable `SetProgramInfo`. At creation it refuses by name:\n  - a number outside 1-9999;\n  - a comment over 40 characters, non-printable or non-ASCII, or containing `( ) % ; *`.\n\n  Chosen: refuse rather than sanitise. Heidenhain and SINUMERIK, which use the comment as the program name, check it against their name rules at post time.\n- **UI:** \"Program number\" and \"Program comment\" fields on the Post page. They commit on Enter or when focus leaves.\n- **MCP:** a new `set_program` tool.\n- **Scripts:** they get a `program` global `{number, numbered, comment}` (`engine::run_program_with`); `programNumber` is kept. Documented in docs/CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md and assets/posts/AGENTS.md.\n- **Per-operation files:** one file per op counts up from the stated number and is refused past O9999. The old code silently clamped instead.\n- **Project file v59:** an optional `program` key. This is a version step, not just an added key, because an older build would drop the key and post O0001, which could overwrite a different program on the control. v58 files load with nothing set.\n\n**Per dialect.** Each rule is cited in its .cps. The manual section references were written from memory, so a maintainer may want to check them against the manuals.\n- **Fanuc, Fanuc Lathe, Mazak:** `O####` (O0001-O9999), then `(<comment or machine name>)`.\n- **Haas:** five-digit `O#####`, written only when a number is set.\n- **Tormach PathPilot:** never an O-word, because LinuxCNC's O words are subroutine and flow-control words. A number goes in the header comment.\n- **Heidenhain ISO:** the comment becomes the program name, `%<name> G71 *`, limited to file-name characters. If only a number is set, it is used as the name.\n- **SINUMERIK:** the comment becomes `%_N_<NAME>_MPF` (letters, digits and `_`; the first two are letters or `_` plus a letter; at most 24 characters). A name that breaks these rules is refused, not renamed. The number goes in a `; PROGRAM n` comment.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/258-program-number.md`.\n\n## How tested\n- **New `program_info` tests (9):**\n  - output is byte-identical in all 7 posts when nothing is set;\n  - each dialect's header with a number and comment, and with a number alone;\n  - post-time refusals;\n  - command validation, undo and redo;\n  - the typed-number parser (accepts `O0012`);\n  - per-op numbering;\n  - a live post writes `O0077 (Lid)`, and undo restores O0001;\n  - round-trip: a v58 file loads with nothing set, and a corrupt value is refused.\n- **Also new:** `mcp_setup::set_program_states_undoes_and_refuses_by_name`, and ui `program_info_tests` (typing into the fields, Ctrl+Z/Ctrl+Y, a refusal).\n- **Gate:** 35 app test binaries (338 tests) pass, including conformance, golden_cl, posting, every post suite, project_roundtrip, commands_undo, mcp and mcp_setup. All camcraft-post tests pass. ui lib passes 378; the one failure is the headless-GPU test, which also fails on this machine without the change. Clippy (post/app/ui, `-D warnings`) is clean. **No golden changed.**\n\n## Not exercised\nA GUI hands-on check, and a run of a numbered program on a control or in the Hub. G-code changes only when a number or comment is set.\n\nChangelog: The document states its program number and comment (Post page, MCP set_program); each post writes it in its own dialect - O-word (Fanuc, Fanuc Lathe, Mazak, Haas), Heidenhain program name, SINUMERIK %_N_..._MPF, PathPilot header comment; project v59 (#258)\n\nRefs #258\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
